---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout route="/privacy/">
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">How we handle your data</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-content">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="content-card">
        <span class="date">Last updated: April 24, 2026</span>

        <p>
          DIRTTIME ("we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and safeguard your information when you use our DIRTTIME mobile application (the "App").
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Scope:</strong> This policy covers the App. Our marketing website at <a href="https://dirttime.xyz/">dirttime.xyz</a> uses limited third-party advertising measurement — see <a href="#website-tracking">Website Tracking</a> below — which does not apply to the App.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Data You Provide</h3>
        <p>When you use DIRTTIME, you may provide the following information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Bike Information:</strong> Details about your motorcycles including make, model, year, current hours, and mileage</li>
          <li><strong>Maintenance Records:</strong> Service logs, maintenance tasks, and completion dates</li>
          <li><strong>Ride Logs:</strong> Information about your rides including hours ridden, distance traveled, and terrain type</li>
          <li><strong>Photos:</strong> Images you choose to associate with your bikes</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Automatically Collected Information</h3>
        <p>
          DIRTTIME does not automatically collect personal information, analytics data, or usage statistics. We do not use any third-party analytics or tracking services.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Storage</h2>

        <h3>Local Storage Only</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>All your data is stored locally on your device.</strong> DIRTTIME does not transmit your bike information, maintenance records, ride logs, or photos to any external servers. Your data remains entirely on your iPhone or iPad.
        </p>
        <p>
          We use Apple's built-in storage systems (AsyncStorage and App Groups for widget functionality) to securely store your data on your device.
        </p>

        <h3>No Cloud Sync</h3>
        <p>
          DIRTTIME does not currently offer cloud synchronization. This means:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your data is not backed up to our servers</li>
          <li>We cannot access, view, or recover your data</li>
          <li>Your data stays private and under your control</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Important:</strong> We recommend using your device's built-in backup features (iCloud Backup or iTunes/Finder backup) to protect against data loss.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

        <p>The App does not integrate with or share data with any third-party services, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Analytics providers</li>
          <li>Advertising networks</li>
          <li>Social media platforms</li>
          <li>Crash reporting services</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="website-tracking">Website Tracking</h2>

        <p>
          Our marketing website (dirttime.xyz) uses X (formerly Twitter) conversion tracking to measure the effectiveness of our advertising on X. This applies only to the website, not to the App.
        </p>
        <p>When you visit the website:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The X Pixel may set cookies in your browser and share browsing data with X.</li>
          <li>X uses this data to attribute ad conversions and may combine it with information from your X account if you have one.</li>
          <li>You can opt out via your <a href="https://twitter.com/settings/account/personalization" target="_blank" rel="noopener">X personalization &amp; data settings</a>, browser "Do Not Track" / cookie controls, or an ad blocker.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The App itself contains no analytics, advertising, or tracking SDKs and does not communicate with X or any other third party.
        </p>

        <h2>Device Permissions</h2>

        <p>DIRTTIME may request the following permissions:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Camera/Photo Library:</strong> Used only if you choose to add photos of your bikes. Photos are stored locally on your device and are never uploaded or shared.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All permissions are optional and the app functions fully without granting them.
        </p>

        <h2>Data Security</h2>

        <p>
          Since all data is stored locally on your device, security is provided by:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Apple's iOS security features and encryption</li>
          <li>Your device passcode, Face ID, or Touch ID protection</li>
          <li>App sandboxing that prevents other apps from accessing DIRTTIME's data</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          DIRTTIME is not directed at children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. Since all data is stored locally and never transmitted, no children's data is collected by us.
        </p>

        <h2>Your Rights</h2>

        <h3>Data Access and Deletion</h3>
        <p>
          Since all data is stored locally on your device, you have complete control over your information:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access:</strong> All your data is visible within the app at any time</li>
          <li><strong>Modification:</strong> You can edit or update any information in the app</li>
          <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> You can delete individual bikes, logs, or tasks within the app. To delete all data, simply uninstall the app from your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Export:</strong> Your data remains on your device and can be preserved through iOS backups</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>

        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the "Last updated" date.
        </p>
        <p>
          We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes. Your continued use of the App after any modifications indicates your acceptance of the updated Privacy Policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact Us</h2>

        <p>
          If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please visit our <a href="/support/">Support page</a> for contact options.
        </p>

        <h2>California Privacy Rights</h2>

        <p>
          If you are a California resident, you have specific rights regarding your personal information under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). Since DIRTTIME stores all data locally on your device and does not collect, sell, or share personal information with third parties, these rights are inherently protected by our privacy-first design.
        </p>

        <h2>European Privacy Rights (GDPR)</h2>

        <p>
          If you are located in the European Economic Area, you have certain rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR). Because DIRTTIME does not collect or process personal data on external servers, and all information remains on your device, you maintain full control over your data at all times.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
